<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sultan bin Muhammad Al Qasimi</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">b. 1939</span> · Also known as Sultan III bin Muhammad Al Qasimi</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sultan">Sultan</a> bin Muhammad <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-qasimi">Al Qasimi</a> has been ruler of Sharjah, one of the United Arab <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emirate">Emirates</a>, since 1972, when he succeeded his brother Khalid after a failed coup. A historian with doctorates from British universities, he wrote The Myth of Arab <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/piracy">Piracy</a> in the Gulf (1986), which disputes the British account of Qasimi piracy. He has made Sharjah a centre of museums, universities and publishing.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sultan-bin-muhammad-al-qasimi.jpg" alt="Sultan bin Muhammad Al Qasimi" width="320" height="211" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Rashed132 · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Official_portrait_Sheikh_Dr_Sultan_bin_Mohammed_Al_Qasimi.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
